मण्डलम् समावेशसारणी ॥
आयातः पदविभाग ।

॰ GENERATED by tools/mkspectables.py from spec/ — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
॰ Re-run the generator whenever a spec table changes: regeneration IS the check,
॰ because nothing else compares this module against spec/ again.
॰
॰ THE EMBED STORE, FILLED FROM THIS LANGUAGE. The four globals `पदविभाग` declares
॰ were filled by the HOST at load — `समावेशसंख्या` is, in that file's own margin,
॰ how many the host filled — so a compiled compiler had no tables at all and could
॰ assemble nothing. Filling them here needs no host.
॰
॰ THE TEXT IS BASE-64 over 64 Devanagari letters, because a source's CODE is pure
॰ Devanagari: across all 20 corpus sources, taking each line's code half, there is
॰ not one character outside Devanagari, space and tab. Encoding rather than escaping
॰ leaves no escape set to derive and no character census to get wrong. The alphabet
॰ excludes `इ` so no pair of letters can spell `इति` and close a literal early, and
॰ excludes the nukta forms, which decompose and would change under normalisation.
॰ `विकोडनम्` is the inverse; the generator decodes every table and compares it byte
॰ for byte against its file before writing, so a wrong table cannot be emitted.

॰ AN EMPTY RUN, NOT ०. `उक्तम् इति` is a run of length zero; `०` is the nil word,
॰ and the interpreter refuses `ॱ दैर्घ्य` on it — caught by the loop's own acceptance
॰ suite, which grades this module by RUNNING it rather than by compiling it.
